# Build context is the repo ROOT (the root is a bun workspace), so this is a
# whitelist rather than a blacklist. The root holds a lot that must never enter
# an image or even the context: a 173 MB nvcrm_backup*.sql dump, .env files,
# and several agent/tooling directories (.claude, .codegraph, .omo, .agents,
# .supermemory) containing broken symlinks — those abort the build outright
# with "invalid file request", not a warning.
#
# Blacklisting them one at a time was whack-a-mole: anything new dropped at the
# root would break the deploy. Exclude everything by default instead.

*

# --- re-include only what the build needs ---
!package.json
!bun.lock
!bunfig.toml
!apps/web
!packages

# The new Hono + Vite stack. These were missing, and the omission was invisible
# for as long as the images were built on the VPS — /root/nuraview-app has no
# .dockerignore, so a VPS build sees the whole tree regardless of this file.
# The first CI build failed instantly on "/deploy/package.app.json: not found".
!apps/api
!apps/app
!i18n
!deploy

# --- prune inside the re-included trees ---
apps/web/node_modules
apps/web/.next
# 375 MB of pg_dump output. Git-ignored, so it was invisible until it showed up
# as 400 MB of Docker build context.
apps/web/backups
apps/web/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/web/.env
apps/web/.env.*
apps/web/tests
apps/web/__tests__
apps/web/playwright-report
apps/web/test-results
apps/web/docs
apps/web/.vercel
apps/web/**/*.md
packages/**/node_modules
packages/**/dist
apps/api/node_modules
apps/app/node_modules
apps/app/dist
apps/api/.env
apps/api/.env.*
apps/app/.env
apps/app/.env.*
apps/**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
